// mecatl driver API: the remote soul-source protocol.
//
// SoulSourceService is the wire seam behind the harness's `prompt.SoulSource`
// (engine/prompt/soul.go): an operator-run driver process serves the
// user-scoped, agent-READ-ONLY persona/"soul" body in place of the local
// soul file. The driver sits at the SAME trust tier as the operator's own
// soul file — operator-configured infrastructure, never model-writable (the
// protocol has no write RPC, upholding the no-write-path invariant).
//
// Driver contract:
//   - LoadSoul returns the persona body, or an EMPTY body for "no soul"
//     (fail-soft: an absent persona is normal, never an error).
//   - The harness RE-VALIDATES the body client-side with the full local soul
//     discipline (byte cap, injection scan, data-fence integrity, trim) — a
//     driver is never trusted to sanitize. A body the validation rejects
//     degrades to no fragment, exactly like a rejected local file.
//   - A LoadSoul fault at harness BUILD time (the selection probe) is FATAL
//     (loud-misconfig posture); a fault at RUN time degrades fail-soft to no
//     fragment with a logged warning.

